      "description": "Drone Insurance Dictionary by SkyWatch.AI Drone Insurance Coverage Plans Drone Insurance Drone Insurance For Canadians Annual Drone Insurance Monthly Drone Insurance Hourly Drone Insurance Agriculture Drone Insurance Drone Insurance for Fleets Support claims FAQ Login Services Brokers Integrations Dictionary Aircraft Insurance Coverage Plans Aircraft Owner's Insurance Aircraft Renter's Insurance Student Pilot Insurance Senior Pilot Insurance Hangar Insurance CFI Insurance Services Brokers Partner with us Support claims Aircraft Owner's FAQ Owner's Sample Policy Aircraft renter's FAQ Company Login Drone Insurance - US Drone Insurance - Canada Aircraft Owner's Insurance Aircraft Renter's Insurance blog Support Contact Us Customer Support Claims Drone Operators Non-Owned Aircraft Claims Owned Aircraft Claims Get a Quote Get a Quote Contact Us Chat with a drone specialist 888-364-5033 support@skywatch.ai Chat with an aviation specialist 888-849-4902 aviationsupport@skywatch.ai Office hours Monday - Friday | 9am - 6pm (EST) Broker Consulting Book a personal meeting with our insurance specialists Schedule Now General Inquiries Thank you! Your submission has been received! Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form. Drone Operator's Insurance Drone Insurance USA Drone Insurance Canada Aircraft Owner's Insurance Aircraft Renter's Insurance Weather Widget The SkyWatch.AI Weather Widget is available through the mobile app flight module and it provides live updates on weather conditions. Dark Sky provides all weather updates as seen through the weather widget. Using the Weather Widget for Flight Preparation Waiver of Subrogation A Waiver of Subrogation is a clause stating that one entity is willing to waive (give up) their rights to subrogate against another entity. Obtaining a Waiver of Subrogation Policy Managment Underwriting Underwriting is the process of reviewing applications for insurance and the information provided by the insured. Essentially underwriting is the risk selection process. Learn More Underwriter The Underwriter is responsible for evaluating and classifying risks and accepting or rejecting an insured's insurance application. Learn More TRIA TRIA refers to the Terrorism Risk Insurance Act. This act is a government sponsored coverage that is placed into insurance policies in order to protect against acts of terrorism. Total Loss A Total Loss refers to damage that occurs in which the property or item insured is damaged beyond repair. Learn More Submit A Claim Recreational Use Recreational Use the UAS shall be used for private and pleasure flights excluding any operation for which a charge is made or excluding any used of the UAS involving the insureds business or employment, or any use as required under FAR 107, 333 Letter or COA. Quote The UAS (unmanned aircrat/drone) shall be used for private and pleasure flights, excluding any operation for which a charge is made or excluding any use of the UAS involving the insured's business or employment, or any use as required under FAR 107, 333 Letter or COA (certificate or waiver or authorization). How do I get a quote? Get a Quote Property Damage Liability Property Damage Liability pays for the damage done to someone else's property as a result of the named insured's operation. Property Damage Property damage insurance provides liability coverage for damage caused to someone else's property. Primary A Primary policy is a policy that pays first in the event of a covered loss. All SkyWatch.AI policies are primary policies. Learn More Premium A Premium is the consideration, (money), paid to the insurance company to issue the policy. - or - The amount paid for an insurance policy. Pre-Booking Pre-Booking is the ability to bind a policy before the official policy start date. Hourly, monthly, and annual policies can be pre-booked up to 60 days in advance in order to obtain proof of insurance. How to pre-book a policy? Get started with SkyWatch.AI Policy Period The Policy Period is the time period, stated on the policy document and Certificate of Insurance, during which the policy provides coverage. Learn how to prebook a policy Policy Number A Policy Number refers to the number given to any active policy. The number is used as a reference and tracking measure. Policy Sample Personal Injury Personal Injury means injury, other than bodily injury or property damage, caused by: false arrest, malicious prosecution, wrongful entry, slander, or violations of privacy. Per Person Per Person refers to the maximum amount available for payment of bodily injury to a single person in any accident, despite what the policy states as the liability limit for bodily injury and property damage claims. Policy Sample Per Occurrence Per Occurrence refers to a limit within the liability limits that puts a cap on the payment for any claim that arises from a single occurrence. Policy Sample Part-107 Certificate A Part 107 Certificate is an FAA issued certification given to drone pilots who have passed a written exam and obtained legal permission to offer professional drone services. Learn more Occurrence Occurrence means an accident, including continuous or repeated exposure to conditions, which results in bodily injury or property damage during the policy period neither expected nor intended from the standpoint of the insured. In the event of continuing or progressively deteriorating damage over any length of time, such damage shall be deemed to be one occurrence, and shall be deemed to occur only when such damage first commences. Policy Sample Non-Contributory Non-Contributory means that the insurance policy must pay losses before other applicable policies kick in while also not seeking contribution from other policies. Learn more Named Insured The Name Insured is an individual(s) whose name appears on the policy's declaration. The Name Insured can also be an organization. Monthly Policy A Monthly Policy is an insurance policy that provides coverage for one",
